Question No: 416. Partition Equal Subset Sum

The Solution is in C++ Language.

Solution:

class Solution {
public:
    bool canPartition(vector<int>& nums) {
        int total = accumulate(nums.begin(), nums.end(), 0);
        if (total % 2 != 0) return false;

        int target = total / 2;
        vector<bool> dp(target + 1, false);
        dp[0] = true;

        for (int n : nums) {
            for (int i = target; i >= n; i--) {
                if (dp[i]) continue;
                if (dp[i - n]) dp[i] = true;
                if (dp[target]) return true;
            }
        }

        return false;        
    }
};


Approach:

The solution uses a Dynamic Programming approach to check whether the array can be divided into two subsets with equal sums. 
First, it calculates the total sum of all elements. If the total sum is odd, equal partition is not possible. 
Otherwise, the target sum for each subset is total / 2.
A boolean DP array is used where dp[i] indicates whether a subset with sum i can be formed. Initially, dp[0] is true. 
For each number, the DP array is updated from right to left to avoid using the same number multiple times. 
If dp[target] becomes true, the array can be partitioned into two equal-sum subsets, so the function returns true; otherwise, it returns false.
